<!--Post: 11691--><!--Time: 1111031423-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11691"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 7:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dennis Mckenzie was right about the name Louise being on the poem &#34;Oh Anna Why Didn&#39;t You Appear&#34; because it is in the &#34;Nightmare in Wichita&#34; book Robert Beattie talked about on KAKE News. The book comes out Monday<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11691-->
<!--Post: 11698--><!--Time: 1111034179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11698"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 8:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Also the book will be $14.00 in stores, and there is a website for it too: <a href="http://www.nightmareinwichita.com" target=_top>http://www.nightmareinwichita.com</a> . <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11698-->
<!--Post: 11716--><!--Time: 1111040532-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11716"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 10:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Megabyte: The link you gave is sort of bizarre. First, it claims BTK dropped from sight a FULL DECADE after he ACTUALLY disappeared from the public. It states, &#34;Then in 1988, he [BTK] vanished...&#34;- WHAT!? BTK in fact &#39;vanished&#39; from sight 10 years before that, in 1978 &#40;or &#39;79&#41;! <BR> <BR>Also the sight is all geared towards selling the book, &#34;Nightmare in Wichita&#34;, but doesn&#39;t tell you whether the book is a Hardback, paperback, &#39;trade-paperback&#39; &#40;that&#39;s a large-size paperback&#41;, or what! Who writes this stuff?! Hopefully the book itself isn&#39;t riddled with these kinds of errors &amp; blatant omissions! <BR> <BR>Victor<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11716-->
<!--Post: 11720--><!--Time: 1111051723-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11720"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 1:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Victor; <BR> <BR>It&#39;s Penguin&#39;s New American Library putting out the book. I have seen many instances of poorly informed copywriters putting out blurbs for books like you pointed out. I noticed it too, but am otherwise reserving judgement. &#40;As in, hoping that the dunderheadedness apparent at that site will not be seen in Mr. Beattie&#39;s book.&#41; <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll also be reviewing the book for blogcritics.org. I&#39;ll let y&#39;all know when that&#39;s up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11720-->
<!--Post: 11744--><!--Time: 1111106761-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11744"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 17, 2005 - 4:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok sorry guys didn&#39;t mean to put the wrong link out, anyways Robert Beattie will be doing book signings in Kansas, and possibly other places check your local book store to see if he is coming there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11744-->
<!--Post: 11766--><!--Time: 1111150303-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11766"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 4:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You can order an autographed copy on the net too.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11766-->
<!--Post: 11802--><!--Time: 1111191030-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11802"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 4:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I suspect the narrative will be more accurate than the marketing campaign. The title seems to suggest it could be describing the latest Freddy Krueger adventure. I prefer &#34;Bound in Terror.&#34; <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11802-->
<!--Post: 11904--><!--Time: 1111373152-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11904"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 6:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the book is going to be a hit, one day till it is released, man I can&#39;t wait to go and pick it up, then I plan on getting it signed I&#39;m going to have to get up early.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11904-->
<!--Post: 11907--><!--Time: 1111373507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11907"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 6:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let me correct myself the book will be in tomorrow or Tuesday.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11907-->
<!--Post: 11933--><!--Time: 1111440866-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11933"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 1:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok at some book stores the book has already came out, I&#39;m going to say this though when the book came in early at the East Borders it sold out in 3 hours!! The Borders that I&#39;m getting my copy from will have it tomorrow, it is best to reserve your copy now I know that all Border&#39;s Stores will give you a maximum reserve of 3 days because of the title.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11933-->
<!--Post: 12015--><!--Time: 1111509316-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12015"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 8:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok I&#39;m waiting on Borders to give me that call that my book is in supossedly it is still on the truck, I can&#39;t wait to get my copy, anyways the book sold out in Atlanta, Georgia!!!!! The book has already hit the best seller list, it is going to be a great read, I&#39;m going to post at least one good excerpt from the book here, one only after that if you want to find out more you will have to buy the book.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12015-->
<!--Post: 12016--><!--Time: 1111509412-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12016"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 8:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy_leaguer I think it would be better to get your book autographed in person.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12016-->
<!--Post: 12027--><!--Time: 1111511078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12027"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 9:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It is in!!!! The long anticipated book is in at my local Borders Store, I will post an excerpt in a hour. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12027-->
<!--Post: 12037--><!--Time: 1111524616-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12037"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 12:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Alright, Megabyte! I can&#39;t wait to hear some of the juicy tidbits in the new book. Extremely hard to believe that after 31 years, this is the only book about BTK! <BR> <BR>We&#39;re all anxiously awaiting those &#34;exerpts&#34;! I&#39;ll probably go out &amp; buy my own soon, based on those.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12037-->
<!--Post: 12046--><!--Time: 1111533356-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12046"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 3:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just inside the door, in the dark, Bulla bumped into something. &#34;I&#39;ve had nightmares about that moment,&#34; he said. He had bumped into the body of Charlie&#39;s eleven year old sister, Josephine. She was wearing only a sweat shirt and socks; her bra was cut in front and dangling. She was hanging from a sewer pipe by her neck. Her panties were above the cord around her ankles and below the cord around her knees.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12046-->
<!--Post: 12076--><!--Time: 1111553913-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12076"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 8:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Meg - This is the cop that everyone slammed under &#34;the first cop to Otero scene&#34; thread. This is his story and he told it on national T.V. I don&#39;t think I&#39;ll buy the book, I feel I&#39;ve already lived it. Unless, he donated a portion of the proceeds to the victims families.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12076-->
<!--Post: 12107--><!--Time: 1111587948-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12107"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 6:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi all, can someone with the book verify that one of the &#34;dudes&#34; was picked up in his car with a duck?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
