<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12252"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 7:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty readin the book right now, stil havenot found the duck lol chapter one, starts out with the Day Wichita Changed, details of January 15, 1974 As Charlie Begins his walk home from school. Danny and Carmen were already at the house, each cradling a parent, it is very sad. I will finish the book later tonight, Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
