<!--Post: 12306--><!--Time: 1111947932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12306"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 10:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know it stinks, supposedly BTK brought a 6 pack to the Nancy Fox residence and waited for her then strangled her when she came home and after she was dead BTK drank the beer and watched her head swell and tongue protrude.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12306-->
<!--Post: 12307--><!--Time: 1111947992-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12307"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 10:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The book I think tells the whole BTK story out the best than just what the news has said.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12307-->
<!--Post: 12323--><!--Time: 1111989523-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12323"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 9:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know most people that read the book have this new appreciation for WPD and their efforts to solve this case. IMO, Beattie did an outstanding job at making WPD look good by saying how many man hours were spent, stories of the &#34;extraordinary measures&#34; like the satelite photos, but at the same time he discreetly pointed out their many incomprehensible mistakes. I think he did this intentionally. He doesn&#39;t want to alienate any of his sources in LE, but he still wants the story told.  <BR> <BR>It seemed to me that over and over again, they were refusing to admit that a serial killer could be involved in the killings. I guess I was expecting to find out that they were downplaying BTK to the public, but behind the scenes they were on top of it. Not so.  There was continued debate over whether the letters were hoaxes.  They did not seem to be conecting the dots.   <BR> <BR>After Vian&#39;s murder Detective Cocking said, &#34;this looks like BTK&#34;. He was immediately scorned and told to &#34;Knock off that sh&#42;&#42;.&#34;  <BR> <BR>After Wegerle&#39;s murder, the Ghostbusters were consulted. Could this be a BTK hit? &#34;They were unanimous in agreement: No.&#34; The conclusion was made &#34;that the husband did it&#34;. They were not looking for another killer. They felt like they had their man. <BR> <BR>One of the most shocking things I read &#40;p.236&#41;- was referring to a breakfast Beattie had with a group of retired WPO on March 23, 2004. Jack Bruce said regarding the elder Joseph Otero, &#34;The ropes on Joseph were the only ones that he could have tied himself. ... Prove that Joseph Otero didn&#39;t murder his family then kill himself, either accidentally or on purpose.&#34; Beattie continues &#34;As we departed, Bruce told me that he agreed with Floyd Hannon. He didn&#39;t think there was a BTK.&#34; This was in 2004 after BTK wrote the letter to the police re-emerging and some WPD still don&#39;t think there is a BTK? To me, this is absolutely unbelievable. <BR> <BR>Even though none of the crime scenes were exactly the same, there were soooo many reasons to link them. Missing key chains, missing Drivers License, in 2 of murders car keys were found on the roof of Dillons and they didn&#39;t connect it?, complicated knots, panty hose, no sexual assault &#40;but sexually motivated&#41;, etc.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve ranted for long enough. I am just in shock. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12323-->
<!--Post: 12326--><!--Time: 1111991128-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12326"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 10:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, I caved and bought two copies of the book. But, only because he dedicated it to the victims, their families and friends. Pretty good, thus far.  <BR> <BR>Itty - it was a duck. I remember when that happened, I was a teenager, and the jokes about this guy were abundant and severe because that song disco duck had just came out. HAAAAA!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12326-->
<!--Post: 12327--><!--Time: 1111991505-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12327"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 10:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow, TULIP! Amazing blunders by the WPD, as you&#39;ve posted from the &#34;NIGHTMARE IN WICHITA&#34; book. I had no idea that the murder victims&#39; keys were tossed onto the roof of a Dillons&#39; store in no less than 2 BTK killings! Nothing strange about that, huh? Happens every day. Ya, right.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12327-->
<!--Post: 12330--><!--Time: 1111997325-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12330"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 28, 2005 - 12:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beattie&#39;s book notes that the Otero&#39;s keys were on the roof of the Dillons.  There was a report on Kake that Dee Davis&#39; keys were found on her roof.   <BR> <BR>From KAKE:  &#34;The house&#39;s phone lines were cut, Dee Davis&#39; was strangled, and her body bound. And there were other strange parts of the murder scene, car keys thrown on the roof, shoes piled in pyramids, an object thrown through the back door.&#34;   <BR> <BR>Sorry about the misinformation that her keys were found on the roof of a Dillons.  I read that on another board.  I should have confirmed it on my own before posting it here. <BR> <BR>The WPD seemed very lazy in the Wegerle case.  She was killed on the same day as Al Stewart&#39;s retirement party.  They found tissue under her nails which was &#34;carefully preserved&#34; but not DNA tested.  You would think they could&#39;ve gotten around to testing it &#40;even 10 or 15 years later&#41; to either implicate or eliminate her husband.  They never did.  Disgraceful. Does the WPD have cold case detectives? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12330-->
<!--Post: 12392--><!--Time: 1112156555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12392"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 8:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just received my copy from Amazon.com this afternoon.   <BR> <BR>On the Introduction page, it says &#34;At one time police concluded that he murdered a New York resident in New Orleans, Louisiana, but they kept that secret.&#34; !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12392-->
<!--Post: 12393--><!--Time: 1112156732-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12393"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 8:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->was Mr. Wegerle charged with his wife&#39;s murder? I never heard anything about that. And if he wasn&#39;t, was anybody?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12393-->
<!--Post: 12394--><!--Time: 1112156877-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12394"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 8:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->and another question...remember the thread about what BTK took from victims? There has been a great deal of speculation on this matter. Apparently, he always took the victims keys/key chain.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12394-->
<!--Post: 12395--><!--Time: 1112156927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12395"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 8:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about Ruth Findley? Geez, I was embarrased for them and how much did they spend on that investigation? Whatever!  <BR> <BR>Ivy - I like your name for the book, it fits really well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12395-->
<!--Post: 12396--><!--Time: 1112157943-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12396"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 8:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is another inaccuracy with regards to the 5000 being swabbed: <BR><a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/da/Dennis_Rader/pdf_files/DNARELEASE.pdf" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/da/Dennis_Rader/pdf_ files/DNARELEASE.pdf</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12396-->
<!--Post: 12402--><!--Time: 1112167891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12402"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 29, 2005 - 11:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR> <BR>I believe the title &#34;Bound in Terror&#34; is more appropriate for this particular case. It describes the modus operandi of the perpetrator and the affect of the crimes on the community of Wichita, Kansas. &#34;Nightmare in Wichita&#34; seems to emphasize the brutality of the crimes and sounds abrupt and unrefined.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12402-->
<!--Post: 12406--><!--Time: 1112171078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12406"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 12:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It also sounds like &#34;Nightmare on Elm Street&#34;, which to me, sounds campy. <BR> <BR>But, good book anyway, even if the title does sound like a Grade-B slasher flik.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12406-->
<!--Post: 12414--><!--Time: 1112199965-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12414"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 8:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Brown tornado, <BR> <BR>No, Mr. Wegerle was never charged, but that was because they didn&#39;t have enough evidence to charge him.  They still thought he did it.  According to the book, they never really looked for anyone else.   <BR> <BR>Mr. Wegerle, on the other hand, hired a PI to try to find out who killed his wife.  Sad, huh?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12414-->
